{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Conduct review of HGV insurance cost and impact on newly qualified HGV drivers",
        "additional_details": "Newly qualified HGV drivers can face thousands of pounds in training, test and medical fees. After that investment, newly qualified drivers can therefore feel immense stress trying to find work as prospective employers often face high insurance costs due to excesses for newly qualified drivers. We think this risks creating an unfair cycle, where drivers cannot gain experience and employers can\u2019t afford to hire them (especially as they may not yet have any experience). We therefore call for a review of HGV insurance costs for newly qualified drivers, to consider how employers can be supported to hire newly qualified drivers and tackle driver shortages.",
        "background": "We call for a review of insurance costs faced by employers seeking to hire newly qualified HGV drivers. We are concerned that high costs may discourage employers from hiring newly qualified drivers, which could lead to barriers to employment and driver shortages.",
